  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The neighbourhood service desk",
    "overview": "FixCity uses a compact Material 3 interface for reporting a problem and following a repair. Navy anchors the identity, muted gold marks the street-pin logo and the home reporting action, and teal carries the shared action style. Warm page backgrounds and plain surface panels keep forms and report lists easy to scan.\n\nCairo covers Arabic and English throughout the app. The public demo states that it uses synthetic data, has no government affiliation and sends no real reports. This is a private student initiative with its own identity. InstaPay supplies partnership context only; its branding is not part of this system.\n\nThis document records the shared rules in [theme.dart](app/lib/theme.dart), [brand.dart](app/lib/brand.dart) and the current Flutter screens. Values written as `px` represent Flutter logical pixels. The light Material container and outline colors come from the installed `ColorScheme.fromSeed` implementation; the app still reads those roles from its theme. Dark variants are explicit where the source overrides them. The sidecar translates components to HTML for inspection; its previews use Cairo when the host has that font available.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Report and Track remain visible actions with distinct labels.",
      "Arabic and English share one type family and follow the locale's direction.",
      "Flat surfaces, outlined fields and text labels carry the hierarchy.",
      "Resident navigation stays separate from staff and district role access."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Action Hierarchy Rule",
        "body": "Use the shared teal action style by default. The home reporting button uses gold within its navy panel; preserve that local pairing.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Status Text Rule",
        "body": "Keep a written status beside its color. Call the shared status helpers with the current brightness instead of copying a status hex into a screen.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Bilingual Type Rule",
        "body": "Keep Cairo and the locale's text direction. Let content wrap and grow with the user's text scale; do not force labels into a fixed text height.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Surface Rule",
        "body": "Keep resting page panels flat. Preserve the framework's focus, hover and pressed feedback when reusing Material controls.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do reuse the shared theme and Material controls before adding a local style.",
      "Do keep Arabic and English labels, direction and text scaling intact.",
      "Do pair report status colors with text and choose the correct dark variant.",
      "Do keep the demo notice and original team attribution visible in their existing places."
